   "CHARACTER SHEET - BlackRock   (bake FOURTH, attach as @image4 - the set of this book)\n\nThe only vertical thing on the flat, and the reader's compass for the whole lap. One flat black\nshape #2E2F2D with a soft brush edge; no rendered granite, no texture, no highlights.\n\nFORM: a standing stone about THREE TIMES the young sandpiper's height, wider at the base,\n  leaning very slightly.\nBASE CRACK: a horizontal split at the foot, a hand's width across, dark inside. This is where\n  the four feathers are planted, and it is the darkest hole in the book.\nLEDGES: THREE stepped shelves running up one flank like stairs, each one shallow, visible from\n  the very first page. Nobody is ever shown climbing them - on page 13 they simply carry one wet\n  footprint each.\nTOP CRACK: a narrow deep cleft in the crown, just wide enough to hold a small down feather\n  upright.\nSHEET: front view with the base crack facing us and the ledges on the right flank / rear view,\n  smaller, ledges hidden / far small view seen from the opposite side of the flat, the whole\n  silhouette one dark mark / a low-angle view from the foot looking up at the crown; plus a\n  SCALE PLATE - SandpiperYoung standing at the base, its head reaching about a third of the way\n  up. Wet ripple marks in the sand ring the base in every view.\nPlain paper, no sky, no other objects. SCENE token: BlackRock."
