   "CHARACTER SHEET - ByreSet   (bake THIRD - the stage and the sound, used on every page)\n\nTHE PLACE, empty of the two leads, exactly as it sits on all fourteen pages: one LONG WOODEN\n  TROUGH down the left wall, 🔴 heaped with clover green at its LEFT END and with bare-paper dry\n  hay at its RIGHT END, the two heaps at the same depth in one vessel so the colours are compared\n  side by side. Mid-floor, one thick post and a low partition. At the right wall a SPLIT STABLE\n  DOOR with only the top half open, and through it one flat clover-green field shape with 0 marks\n  inside and a low wall as 3 strokes. On a rafter, one tin bucket. Underfoot, straw as at most 25\n  short strokes. Walls = at most 14 block outlines, 0 interior texture. Above and behind: bare\n  paper.\n🔴 THE THREE BACK-STALL COWS: cut ONE cow silhouette and repeat it THREE times in a row - same\n  outline, same size, same spacing, ink contour only, 0 patches, 0 eyes, 0 marks inside. Draw the\n  row twice: CHEWING (jaw offset to one side) and STOPPED (jaw level, page 5 only). They never\n  turn, never look and never change.\n🔴 THE WALL SOUND PLATE - draw the same stretch of wall three times:\n  A · silent: 0 arcs.\n  B · a short noise: FIVE thick ink arcs springing off the stone face and curving away from it,\n    all struck from the wall, none from the floor, none reaching into the room's middle.\n  C · a long noise: NINE arcs, longer and further apart, and the bucket doubled into two short\n    positions. 🔴 In B and C nothing marks a source - no puff, no dotted trail, no motion line at\n    any animal. Put B and C side by side and check that an arc cannot be traced back to anywhere.\n🔴 ONE FLY: a single fly as 3 ink strokes plus a short looping flight line, drawn once here at\n  actual size. It is on every page and it is always the same fly.\n0 lettering, 0 numerals, 0 signs. SCENE token: ByreSet."
