   "CHARACTER SHEET - RoosterOld   (bake this FOURTH, attach as @image4)\n\nMedium: STYLE ANCHOR changjak-finishshift - opaque gouache on warm laid paper, visible brush\nmarks, flat light, no rendering.\n\nFACE: an old rooster. 🔴 THE COMB IS FOLDED OVER to one side and stays folded on every page. Beak\nshort and blunt, one small round dark dot per eye, no whites, no eyebrows. When he calls the beak\nopens and 🔴 THE CHEST DROPS BACK before the sound gets out - that half-collapse is his signature.\nPLUMAGE: painted as one mass with at most 9 feather-edge strokes in total. 🔴 ONLY TWO TAIL\nFEATHERS LEFT, both drooping. No barbs, no pattern, no down.\nBUILD: small, upright, two feet always. Toes grip whatever he stands on and that grip is drawn -\nhe is the only one whose weight moves things (a treadle, a shelf edge). Wings are not hands: they\nopen for balance and never grasp.\nCLOTHES: none.\nDISTINGUISHING: the SMALL UPRIGHT of the four, and the only one drawn from above his own eye line -\nhe works higher than the dog and lower than the cat.\nREFERENCE SHEET: 4 views on bare warm paper, evenly spaced, no ground line -\n(1) standing on one foot on a wide board, neck pulled in (posture 1 - his idle place);\n(2) 🔴 neck stretched straight up, beak wide open, chest half fallen back, toes clenched\n    (posture 2);\n(3) 🔴 standing on a narrow shelf edge, neck pushed short and forward, beak tip touching a small\n    opening, chest emptied, both tail feathers flicked back (posture 3);\n(4) standing square in front of something, chest pushed forward and swollen, beak closed\n    (posture 4).\nNO letters, numbers or symbols anywhere on the sheet.\nSCENE token: RoosterOld.",
